# Per-deployment runtime state written by the Go server (regenerated at runtime, must not
# be committed): the plug-sweep savings counter and the learned-baseline model snapshot.
server/data/plug-state.json
server/data/baseline-model.json
server/data/room-dynamics.json
server/data/load-history.json

# THIS DEPLOYMENT'S OWN building, ontology and site calibration.
#
# The repository tracks building-data.json, brick-ontology.json and programme-library.json
# as the defaults a fresh clone boots on. But the running system REWRITES the first two
# (the blueprint importer replaces them on deploy and rollback) and calibrating the third
# is its entire documented purpose — so on a shared repo those tracked files put every
# collaborator's `git pull` in conflict with their own building, and every obvious way out
# of that conflict deletes it.
#
# So the runtime reads and writes `*.local.json` instead (server/simulation/datapath.go):
# git carries the default, each deployment keeps its own copy here, and a pull can no
# longer touch it. Delete a .local.json to fall back to the repository's version.
server/data/*.local.json

# Blueprint deploy/rollback snapshots and the audit log — one deployment's history, not
# something another clone should inherit.
server/data/backups/
server/data/building-audit.log

# Dashboard production build. Regenerated by `npm run build`, and Vite hashes every asset
# filename, so each collaborator's build produces a different set of tracked files and a
# guaranteed pull conflict over artifacts nobody reviews. Build it, don't commit it.
dashboard/dist/

# Dependency tree — 20k files and 363 MB in git history, and the source of the
# repository's vulnerability alerts. Reproducible from package-lock.json.
node_modules/

# Broker credentials and the engine's admin token, generated by server/setup-mqtt-auth.sh.
# These are the building's keys: the passwd file authenticates every node, and the admin
# token authorizes every command that can close a relay.
server/mosquitto/passwd
server/.env
.env

# Local bench overrides (e.g. anonymous broker). Never commit: the committed
# compose file is authenticated by default and must stay that way.
server/docker-compose.override.yml
docker-compose.override.yml
build/
.tools/
.agents/
